= Bioinformatics =

== Scope ==
Bioinformatics covers computational methods for storing, organizing, analyzing, interpreting, and reproducing work with biological information. It is intrinsically interdisciplinary across biology, computer science, statistics/mathematics, and data/information systems.

== Includes ==
Sequence analysis and alignment, biological databases, genome/transcriptome analysis, annotation, similarity search, phylogenetic computation, structural bioinformatics, biological workflow systems, computational reproducibility/provenance, and related algorithms or infrastructure where biological data is central.

== Excludes / boundary ==
Not all computational biology, statistics, software engineering, or biological data work needs this category. Use it when the computational treatment of biological information is a defining feature. General biological concepts belong primarily in Biology; general algorithms/software concepts belong primarily in Computer science, with multiple category membership used when both contexts matter.

== Category role ==
'''Interdisciplinary field/subfield navigation category.''' Bioinformatics is not currently a separate controlled top-level Domain; its portal is deliberately polyhierarchical.

